  "weakest_point": "prim_lc_sync is the first life-cycle typed synchronizer gate and introduces lc_ctrl_pkg plus prim_sec_anchor_buf output buffering. The first gate fixes NumCopies=2, AsyncOn=1, and ResetValueIsOn=0, so it does not prove all life-cycle encodings, ResetValueIsOn=1, AsyncOn=0, all NumCopies values, prim_lc_sender behavior, prim_sec_anchor_flop behavior, full CDC correctness, raw full-state equality, or zero-initialized GPU correctness.",
  "why_this_target": [
    "the fifteenth primitive review accepted only Width=8 and NumChecks=2 for generic prim_multibit_sync",
    "prim_lc_sync is the narrowest next step that targets the remaining life-cycle typed sync gap",
    "it reuses the already active prim_flop_2sync path and adds only lc_ctrl_pkg typed wiring plus prim_sec_anchor_buf output buffering",
    "it is narrower than prim_sync_reqack because it avoids a two-clock request/acknowledge FSM",
    "it is narrower than prim_lc_sender because it does not introduce prim_sec_anchor_flop in the first life-cycle typed gate",
    "it should reuse the shared Verilator/GPU/runtime flow without target-specific runtime hooks"
  ],
